833:Let us recall that we consider reduced minimal and reduced camera-minimal \PLoneP{}s in \emph{three views}, since there is only one such \PLoneP{} in two views, namely the five-points problem. 
835:To argue this, we first notice that free lines cannot occur in a reduced \PLoneP{} in two views. Indeed, if there was a free line -- no matter if it is observed in both views, one view, or not at all -- we could forget the free line both in 3D and in the images to reduce the \PLoneP{} (i.e. forgetting the free line satisfies Definition~\ref{def:reduced-PL1P} of reducibility).
