The parts of Theorem~\ref{thm:reducedMinimalLooks} (and Theorem~\ref{thm:danglingPins}) addressing points with three or more pins have already been proven in Lemma~\ref{lem:complete-pin-removal}.
To find all ways of how free lines and points with at most two pins can be observed by reduced camera-minimal \PLoneP{}s in three views, 
it is enough (by Lemma~\ref{lem:tableComplete}) 
to gather the non-reducible observed features in Table~\ref{tab:proofAllTheorems}.
Among those, the ones marked as minimal are listed in Theorem~\ref{thm:reducedMinimalLooks}, the others in Theorem~\ref{thm:danglingPins}.
