The abstract’s “complete classification” is not itself a usable hardness result. The paper’s actual computational split is emerging: signatures/minimality are handled by finite-field Jacobian rank checks, while camera degrees are obtained by numerical monodromy. I’m now checking whether a native reconstruction family can retain a short structural route while its standard mechanical route is genuinely large enough for Track B; otherwise this paper must be rejected rather than mislabeled Track A.
