The paper’s reduction theorems collapse every scalable PL1P instance to a bounded reduced core with unchanged degree. Native certificates are produced either by fast finite-field Jacobian rank computation or by numerical homotopy, with no distinct compact no-tool route. Thus H fails for both Track A and Track B, although G and V are feasible. This matches the paper’s finite classification and solver-based degree computations. [Paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.05015)

The reviewable rejection—including theorem references and the measured 458,260-operation mechanical-versus-compact comparison—is in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.05015/REJECTED.md).
